1
00:00:11,407 --> 00:00:14,493
FROM ME TO YOU 2ND SEASON

2
00:01:04,502 --> 00:01:05,336
Huh?

3
00:01:06,003 --> 00:01:07,046
Where's Sawako?

4
00:01:07,129 --> 00:01:13,052
Oh, she left a while ago to head off
to her school festival's after-party.

5
00:01:13,135 --> 00:01:14,053
Is that so?

6
00:01:14,720 --> 00:01:18,474
It's strange... Our little girl
sure does go out a lot these days...

7
00:01:18,557 --> 00:01:22,228
Well, you know if she gets a
boyfriend, it is only going to get worse,

8
00:01:22,311 --> 00:01:23,145
honey.

9
00:01:32,488 --> 00:01:34,698
Yeah, you're right. Because once she finds
someone to marry she not going to be here

10
00:01:34,782 --> 00:01:35,658
at all.

11
00:01:37,409 --> 00:01:42,289
I think you might be getting a
little ahead of yourself, dear.

12
00:01:46,794 --> 00:01:51,549
So what do you think,
Yano-chin? Did she get there before him?

13
00:01:51,632 --> 00:01:56,178
Who knows? I bet she beat him! I mean,
they did plan to meet up so they could

14
00:01:56,262 --> 00:02:00,975
walk to the party together, after all.

15
00:02:01,267 --> 00:02:02,393
Am I late?

16
00:02:07,231 --> 00:02:08,440
Not really.

17
00:02:14,947 --> 00:02:18,951
I wonder if that's actually
what's happening right now!

18
00:02:19,034 --> 00:02:21,954
- Wish I was there to tease 'em!
- What if neither of them shows up?

19
00:02:22,037 --> 00:02:24,748
Ooo, I'd punch Kazehaya so hard!

20
00:02:48,981 --> 00:02:52,818
I thought I was sneaking a peek at
him, but I was caught red-handed!

21
00:02:52,902 --> 00:02:55,696
What's with that
reaction?! It's kinda hurtful...

22
00:02:55,821 --> 00:02:57,823
I... I'm so sorry!

23
00:02:59,658 --> 00:03:01,285
It's just... I'm nervous.

24
00:03:02,369 --> 00:03:03,954
Yeah, I'm nervous, too.

25
00:03:06,457 --> 00:03:07,666
It makes me blush.

26
00:03:21,388 --> 00:03:22,806
We're the same.

27
00:03:26,936 --> 00:03:27,728
I like you!

28
00:03:28,938 --> 00:03:30,606
They're the same, right?

29
00:03:31,148 --> 00:03:33,859
Kazehaya I want your everything...

30
00:03:36,779 --> 00:03:37,947
This is like a dream!

31
00:03:38,614 --> 00:03:39,531
Sa~wa~ko!

32
00:03:41,367 --> 00:03:44,078
- They were just holding hands there!
- Seriously? But I thought

33
00:03:44,161 --> 00:03:46,163
they were holding each other?

34
00:03:46,247 --> 00:03:48,540
- Nah, it was only the hands!
- You sure?

35
00:03:48,624 --> 00:03:51,794
- What?! Wait, that really happened?!
- I wish I could have seen that! Wow!

36
00:03:51,877 --> 00:03:55,172
The distance was more like this...

37
00:03:56,131 --> 00:03:57,383
- K-Kazehaya!
- K-Kazehaya!

38
00:03:57,758 --> 00:04:00,803
Oh, hey, Kazehaya! Since not everyone was
there, I decided to put on a reenactment

39
00:04:00,886 --> 00:04:01,887
for 'em!

40
00:04:04,974 --> 00:04:08,519
That's right! There was also
that thing that happened yesterday--

41
00:04:08,602 --> 00:04:12,064
Hey, Joe... Do you mind if
I punch you real quick?

42
00:04:12,147 --> 00:04:15,651
Wait, are you saying
what I think you're saying?!

43
00:04:15,734 --> 00:04:18,529
Whoa, no way! Is it true,
Kazehaya? Do you actually like Sadako?

44
00:04:18,612 --> 00:04:21,407
- What do they mean by you're "the same"?
- Does "Like a dream" mean a

45
00:04:21,490 --> 00:04:24,118
nightmare? Or a good dream?

46
00:04:24,201 --> 00:04:26,829
- I'm pretty sure they walked in together!
- Are you two are gonna start going out?

47
00:04:26,912 --> 00:04:29,748
Oh no... Why is this happening?
Where do I even begin? Well, I...

48
00:04:30,040 --> 00:04:33,168
To answer that last question...

49
00:04:35,462 --> 00:04:36,297
Yeah.

50
00:04:40,217 --> 00:04:41,719
Wait a sec... For real?!

51
00:04:43,512 --> 00:04:46,390
- That wasn't a joke, right?
- How'd you snag Kazehaya,

52
00:04:46,473 --> 00:04:48,225
- Sadako? What's your secret?
- Was it Sorcery?

53
00:04:48,309 --> 00:04:49,435
No, stop!

54
00:04:54,440 --> 00:04:57,359
It's me... who is head over heels for her.

55
00:05:03,657 --> 00:05:07,578
It's alright! This is what
we've all been waiting for...

56
00:05:10,748 --> 00:05:12,833
You understand that... don't you?

57
00:05:16,253 --> 00:05:17,838
I...I feel the same.

58
00:05:21,175 --> 00:05:26,263
You made me sweat for a
second there! I'm so relieved!

59
00:05:29,683 --> 00:05:33,187
- It actually looks serious!
- It actually looks serious!

60
00:05:33,270 --> 00:05:35,230
- We don't just look serious, we--
- Amazing!

61
00:05:36,815 --> 00:05:38,901
Sadako, you're incredible!

62
00:05:38,984 --> 00:05:40,527
Dating the Kazehaya?

63
00:05:40,611 --> 00:05:42,112
I always knew that
Sadako was the real deal!

64
00:05:42,196 --> 00:05:43,322
Bless me!

65
00:05:44,114 --> 00:05:44,990
Me too!

66
00:05:46,742 --> 00:05:48,494
- Please grant me a significant other, too.
- Please grant me a significant other, too.

67
00:05:48,577 --> 00:05:50,913
It's not like that!

68
00:05:50,996 --> 00:05:53,374
Well, this sure started
something weird, didn't it?

69
00:05:53,457 --> 00:05:56,085
I guess it's okay since
they all look pretty happy.

70
00:05:56,168 --> 00:05:58,796
- I can't answer prayers!
- Congrats on taking 6th place in

71
00:05:58,879 --> 00:06:02,633
- the school festival, Class 2-D!
- Cheers!

72
00:06:05,386 --> 00:06:06,595
Is this real?

73
00:06:08,097 --> 00:06:09,973
...I can't believe it.

74
00:06:11,308 --> 00:06:12,142
No...

75
00:06:14,645 --> 00:06:16,563
I want to believe.

76
00:06:16,647 --> 00:06:18,148
- Sa wako!
- Sa wako!

77
00:06:27,074 --> 00:06:28,033
It's okay...

78
00:06:29,952 --> 00:06:30,786
I'm...

79
00:06:34,540 --> 00:06:36,083
I'm not a burden.

80
00:06:45,509 --> 00:06:46,176
Ugh, dammit!

81
00:06:47,177 --> 00:06:48,512
My top-grade sushi!

82
00:06:50,139 --> 00:06:53,517
- Seriously? That's so cute!
- Wait a sec...

83
00:06:54,184 --> 00:06:57,521
Jeez, it's just, Miura.
Didn't expect to see you.

84
00:06:58,313 --> 00:07:00,357
- Isn't that Pin?
- I see you're with girls from another

85
00:07:00,441 --> 00:07:02,484
class. It's a little late to be out here
flirting on the beach, isn't it?

86
00:07:02,568 --> 00:07:04,528
What're the odds?

87
00:07:04,611 --> 00:07:08,532
Shouldn't you be at that
after-party or something?

88
00:07:08,615 --> 00:07:12,536
Normally, I would've tried to go, but
I got a better invite to come out here.

89
00:07:12,619 --> 00:07:15,706
What about you, Mr. Arai? Don't tell me
you came to a place like this to drink

90
00:07:15,789 --> 00:07:18,709
- alone!
- Oh no, how depressing...

91
00:07:19,460 --> 00:07:20,043
Quiet, you!

92
00:07:20,919 --> 00:07:25,132
- Hey, that's our class!
- What the...

93
00:07:27,968 --> 00:07:32,181
They're... in the honeymoon phase...
Mr. "My-Feelings-Finally-Reached".

94
00:07:32,931 --> 00:07:34,183
Oh, Sadako! Hey...

95
00:07:35,225 --> 00:07:37,728
I'm glad to see everything
worked out! What a relief!

96
00:07:37,811 --> 00:07:40,314
Thank you so much, Master...

97
00:07:42,024 --> 00:07:45,569
- Oh! And Kazehaya... Come here for a sec.
- Huh? Let's have a little chat, shall we?

98
00:07:45,652 --> 00:07:49,198
- What do you even want?
- It won't take long!

99
00:07:49,281 --> 00:07:51,992
What's with those two?

100
00:07:52,367 --> 00:07:55,204
- Have they always been that close?
- Hey, Kuronuma. Shh... over here.

101
00:07:57,289 --> 00:08:02,002
Don't make her cry anymore.
It's not doing her any good.

102
00:08:02,085 --> 00:08:07,174
Remember? That day when Sadako was
crying in the schoolyard... Know why?

103
00:08:08,842 --> 00:08:11,845
She was really upset because she
thought there was someone else that you

104
00:08:11,929 --> 00:08:15,265
- liked already.
- What? Why?

105
00:08:15,349 --> 00:08:17,935
Uh, because someone told her?

106
00:08:18,018 --> 00:08:19,019
Who did?

107
00:08:19,603 --> 00:08:21,063
Oh, that would be me!

108
00:08:23,315 --> 00:08:26,693
- So then it was your fault after all!
- Ya got me!

109
00:08:28,529 --> 00:08:31,823
Also... ...it's not Sadako, it's Sawako!

110
00:08:31,907 --> 00:08:33,075
Yeah? You sure?

111
00:08:33,659 --> 00:08:35,786
So I can call her Sawako, then?

112
00:08:37,538 --> 00:08:38,539
Sadako's fine.

113
00:08:40,374 --> 00:08:42,793
I use it as a term of endearment.

114
00:08:51,927 --> 00:08:54,346
About yesterday... Did you...

115
00:08:54,429 --> 00:08:56,265
...tell him everything?

116
00:08:56,348 --> 00:09:00,686
- Yester... Oh! That's right!
- Shh! You're being too loud!

117
00:09:00,769 --> 00:09:05,232
- Pin!
- Hey, Shota, come over here for a sec.

118
00:09:06,567 --> 00:09:09,987
- What do you want?
- So, you two are going out?

119
00:09:10,070 --> 00:09:10,946
Y-Yeah.

120
00:09:12,364 --> 00:09:16,159
Oh really? You sure you're not the
only one who thinks that's the case?

121
00:09:16,243 --> 00:09:20,038
Huh? -Did you make sure to properly say
"Please go out with me" loud and clear for

122
00:09:20,122 --> 00:09:23,458
- her?
- No... but I know she--

123
00:09:23,959 --> 00:09:27,462
You better think again! Does she look
like someone who would fully understand

124
00:09:27,546 --> 00:09:30,257
something so indirect?

125
00:09:31,383 --> 00:09:34,052
Go on, ask her right now!

126
00:09:38,307 --> 00:09:42,311
He's right. The way I asked
her earlier isn't enough.

127
00:09:44,062 --> 00:09:45,105
Kuronuma.

128
00:09:45,814 --> 00:09:46,648
Yes?

129
00:09:48,317 --> 00:09:50,027
Will you please marry me?!

130
00:09:51,153 --> 00:09:51,987
Ma...

131
00:09:52,487 --> 00:09:53,322
...rry?!

132
00:09:53,947 --> 00:09:55,907
Juuuust kidding.

133
00:09:58,160 --> 00:10:02,080
- Go home! You're so annoying!
- Oh? So that's how you're gonna treat

134
00:10:02,164 --> 00:10:05,709
- the person who got you this far? Come on...
- Puh...

135
00:10:07,210 --> 00:10:08,045
Puh?

136
00:10:08,837 --> 00:10:11,923
Please give me time to consider.

137
00:10:13,675 --> 00:10:15,302
Kuronuma, I...!

138
00:10:19,473 --> 00:10:20,307
Huh?

139
00:10:20,557 --> 00:10:22,976
I need a little more
time to think about it

140
00:10:23,060 --> 00:10:25,729
Wait, you've got it all wrong!

141
00:10:25,812 --> 00:10:29,066
That's not good. Are you sure you
don't want to chase after her to expla--

142
00:10:29,149 --> 00:10:33,153
Do you realize what you did?! Huh?!
You think you're funny or something?!

143
00:10:33,320 --> 00:10:37,532
In the worse case, I guess,
she'll say "yes" to the proposal.

144
00:10:39,409 --> 00:10:43,288
Considering it seems like she doesn't
really get jokes. So, If she took it

145
00:10:43,372 --> 00:10:47,250
seriously and then you told her it was a
lie, she'd probably be hurt... it might even

146
00:10:47,334 --> 00:10:49,670
make her depressed!

147
00:10:51,296 --> 00:10:54,299
You're in a real pickle! Guess it doesn't
matter if you're dating or not now... So if

148
00:10:54,383 --> 00:10:58,428
this ends up going south... It's all over!

149
00:11:02,557 --> 00:11:04,309
Well, good luck, Shota!

150
00:11:09,564 --> 00:11:10,816
Hello? Oh, hi Dad.

151
00:11:12,693 --> 00:11:13,902
Uh-huh, I'm okay.

152
00:11:15,362 --> 00:11:18,824
Mm, I'll try not to be
home too late tonight.

153
00:11:18,907 --> 00:11:20,575
Yeah. Oh, and... if I...

154
00:11:23,787 --> 00:11:25,414
A-Actually, never mind!

155
00:11:26,123 --> 00:11:27,791
Hm? What is it? Tell me.

156
00:11:31,336 --> 00:11:35,424
If I ever got married to
someone in the future...

157
00:11:35,507 --> 00:11:37,467
...how would you feel?

158
00:11:39,636 --> 00:11:42,848
Uh, on second thought,
forget I said anything!

159
00:11:46,768 --> 00:11:49,229
Huh? Darling, is something the matter?

160
00:12:03,368 --> 00:12:04,286
Kuronuma.

161
00:12:10,834 --> 00:12:11,752
Kazehaya...

162
00:12:17,591 --> 00:12:18,467
Listen...

163
00:12:19,634 --> 00:12:25,307
I think you've... got it wrong. Uh...
um... a-about the marriage thing.

164
00:12:27,517 --> 00:12:28,643
K-Kazehaya...

165
00:12:29,394 --> 00:12:32,939
Are you trying to say that the mention of
marriage earlier was a misunderstanding?

166
00:12:33,023 --> 00:12:36,359
Yeah. Punch me if you want.

167
00:12:37,402 --> 00:12:41,198
No! That's not necessary at all! I
mean... I doubt anyone would have taken that

168
00:12:41,281 --> 00:12:44,242
seriously, let alone me.

169
00:12:45,118 --> 00:12:49,247
And it was obvious Mr. Arai was
the one who actually said it.

170
00:12:49,372 --> 00:12:50,207
Whaa...?

171
00:12:51,583 --> 00:12:52,334
Uh-huh.

172
00:12:53,376 --> 00:12:56,087
OM dramatic relievedshocked reax

173
00:12:59,424 --> 00:13:01,802
PLEASE LET ME IMAGINE IT

174
00:13:03,220 --> 00:13:05,388
I... I wanna curl up and die.

175
00:13:07,140 --> 00:13:08,892
Sorry... It's my fault...

176
00:13:10,519 --> 00:13:12,562
I caused some confusion.

177
00:13:12,646 --> 00:13:15,607
You see... all I wanted was to picture it.

178
00:13:16,149 --> 00:13:19,569
Then I quickly realized that it was
something I could picture by using my

179
00:13:19,653 --> 00:13:21,154
imagination.

180
00:13:23,615 --> 00:13:26,868
Because of that... I think I've become a
little greedy when it comes to those kinds

181
00:13:26,952 --> 00:13:28,203
of things.

182
00:13:35,877 --> 00:13:39,089
I should have asked
properly. You deserve that.

183
00:13:46,805 --> 00:13:48,849
I want to do this right...

184
00:13:48,932 --> 00:13:50,976
...because I know if I don't,

185
00:13:51,935 --> 00:13:53,520
... we can't move forward.

186
00:13:56,022 --> 00:13:58,441
So please, will you go out with me?

187
00:14:00,026 --> 00:14:00,819
I promise...

188
00:14:01,736 --> 00:14:03,697
...I'll always care for you.

189
00:14:06,741 --> 00:14:07,659
Always...?

190
00:14:09,244 --> 00:14:10,120
Always?

191
00:14:12,581 --> 00:14:13,415
Yes!

192
00:14:26,219 --> 00:14:28,972
I... I have something really important
that I'd like to tell you too, Kazehaya.

193
00:14:29,055 --> 00:14:29,931
Y-Yeah?

194
00:14:32,142 --> 00:14:36,605
- Please don't hate me for it.
- I couldn't... say whatever you need to.

195
00:14:37,147 --> 00:14:38,023
Well I...

196
00:14:38,899 --> 00:14:43,069
I can't look at you anymore... without
having some kind of ulterior motive in

197
00:14:43,153 --> 00:14:47,365
- mind!
- Kuronuma... how could I hate

198
00:14:47,532 --> 00:14:51,119
you for something like that?!

199
00:14:51,578 --> 00:14:55,540
Well, aren't they adorable. We
didn't have anything to worry about.

200
00:14:55,624 --> 00:14:58,126
But man, I'm jealous!

201
00:14:58,209 --> 00:15:00,837
Careful. Your real
feelings are showing, Yano-chin.

202
00:15:00,921 --> 00:15:03,548
I mean, it's just because I
think they're such a great match.

203
00:15:03,632 --> 00:15:04,466
Yeah.

204
00:15:06,092 --> 00:15:08,470
I feel kind of bad for saying he's
the person who understood her the least.

205
00:15:08,553 --> 00:15:10,639
Said that to who?

206
00:15:14,225 --> 00:15:15,602
C'mon, who?

207
00:15:15,810 --> 00:15:17,020
K-Kazehaya.

208
00:15:17,854 --> 00:15:18,688
When?

209
00:15:19,397 --> 00:15:23,860
Around when Sawako and
Kazehaya were becoming awkward...

210
00:15:23,944 --> 00:15:28,490
- So it was you!
- I-I'm sorry, Yano-chin!

211
00:15:28,573 --> 00:15:33,161
They turned out okay in the end,
so why don't you just let her go?

212
00:15:33,244 --> 00:15:38,124
Shut your stupid mouth! Don't you have
some girls you could be flirting with?

213
00:15:38,208 --> 00:15:40,043
Hey, Yano-chin!

214
00:15:40,126 --> 00:15:41,836
Oh! Is Class C having
their after-party too?

215
00:15:41,920 --> 00:15:42,754
Yup.

216
00:15:44,255 --> 00:15:46,549
Where's Sadako? Is she
in her honeymoon phase?

217
00:15:46,633 --> 00:15:48,969
Right on the mark, Chigusa.

218
00:15:49,052 --> 00:15:51,388
Oooh. Nice! Sadako.

219
00:16:30,010 --> 00:16:30,844
So, then...

220
00:16:32,387 --> 00:16:34,139
it wasn't a dream!

221
00:16:35,932 --> 00:16:41,062
It's strange... It still feels like
one even though I know it's not.

222
00:16:43,481 --> 00:16:46,151
But for me to put this much effort
in before before going to bed means...

223
00:16:46,234 --> 00:16:48,319
Uh... Are you done?

224
00:16:51,448 --> 00:16:52,782
...It's reality.

225
00:16:53,783 --> 00:16:54,909
I like you!

226
00:16:55,535 --> 00:16:57,996
So please, will you go out with me?

227
00:16:59,706 --> 00:17:00,957
I'm so happy.

228
00:17:02,792 --> 00:17:04,044
This is real.

229
00:17:18,600 --> 00:17:20,852
What the... What is this?!

230
00:17:20,935 --> 00:17:23,646
Uh... They all want consultations...

231
00:17:23,730 --> 00:17:27,317
- With black magic?!
- Sadako made Kazehaya hers?

232
00:17:27,400 --> 00:17:32,989
From what I heard, Kazehaya's eyes
were glowing red when he asked her out!

233
00:17:34,032 --> 00:17:35,825
I... like you. I like you!

234
00:17:37,827 --> 00:17:41,539
- Scary!
- He must be completely under her spell!

235
00:17:41,623 --> 00:17:45,210
- Oh wow! That makes so much sense!
- Incredible!

236
00:17:45,835 --> 00:17:46,711
Sadako!

237
00:17:47,337 --> 00:17:48,171
Huh?

238
00:17:51,174 --> 00:17:53,218
Don't push! Wait your turn!

239
00:17:53,301 --> 00:17:55,637
- Hey! Hold on, guys!
- Please!

240
00:17:55,720 --> 00:18:00,141
- What are you all lining up for?
- Wait, really? 'Cause everyone who

241
00:18:00,225 --> 00:18:04,646
visited the consultation booth ended up
getting to date their crush!

242
00:18:04,729 --> 00:18:06,189
Wait seriously?

243
00:18:06,272 --> 00:18:09,109
She's feared, she's
worshipped, she's a god now.

244
00:18:09,192 --> 00:18:12,028
You should start charging money.

245
00:18:12,112 --> 00:18:14,864
I'm... pretty sure that's fraud.

246
00:18:14,948 --> 00:18:19,452
Honestly... if that's the perk from just
being around her... then we would have super

247
00:18:19,536 --> 00:18:22,372
hot boyfriends already!

248
00:18:24,124 --> 00:18:27,877
Yeah, pretty much! Like, come on! The
only guys around us are like total idiots!

249
00:18:27,961 --> 00:18:32,173
Oh well As long as she
didn't get picked on, I'm glad.

250
00:18:32,257 --> 00:18:35,927
- Looks like we had nothing to worry about.
- Can you lend me an item for protection?!

251
00:18:36,010 --> 00:18:38,221
Maybe a shikigami!

252
00:18:40,265 --> 00:18:41,975
Oh no... Don't tell me...

253
00:18:43,226 --> 00:18:46,855
...Please tell me Kazehaya doesn't
believe that I have magical powers?

254
00:18:46,938 --> 00:18:49,899
Really? You're sayin'this now?

255
00:18:49,983 --> 00:18:52,986
Oh I'm too tired to bother at this point.

256
00:18:54,028 --> 00:18:55,071
I told you...!

257
00:18:55,155 --> 00:18:58,783
It's not like that at all!
I've liked Kuronuma for a while!

258
00:18:58,867 --> 00:19:01,661
So the story's for
real? It's not made up?

259
00:19:01,744 --> 00:19:04,539
- Are you even listening?
- Is it at least true that

260
00:19:04,622 --> 00:19:07,458
- your eyes were glowing red?
- Oh, speak of the devil!

261
00:19:10,086 --> 00:19:10,920
Good...

262
00:19:11,296 --> 00:19:12,130
Good...

263
00:19:12,463 --> 00:19:13,840
- Good morning.
- Good morning.

264
00:19:13,923 --> 00:19:15,508
You all hear that?

265
00:19:15,592 --> 00:19:18,469
He's liked Sawako for a while now!

266
00:19:18,553 --> 00:19:21,264
That's right! It was a
dream-come-true for him!

267
00:19:21,347 --> 00:19:24,434
Hey! What makes you
think you know about--

268
00:19:24,517 --> 00:19:27,604
Now that our class, and all the other
classes are actually together in one

269
00:19:27,687 --> 00:19:31,024
location... ...why not make it clear, so
no one ever bothers you about it again?

270
00:19:31,107 --> 00:19:34,444
Say loud and proud,
what Sawako is to you!

271
00:19:34,527 --> 00:19:36,821
Poke, poke, poke, poke,
poke, poke, poke, poke.

272
00:19:47,081 --> 00:19:47,999
My girlfriend!

273
00:19:49,792 --> 00:19:51,211
I'm his girlfriend?!

274
00:19:51,794 --> 00:19:53,296
Ooh! Finally, the naked truth!

275
00:19:54,756 --> 00:19:58,676
Hearing him use that word
makes everything seem so real!

276
00:19:59,469 --> 00:20:03,514
Look, I... I'm just
overwhelmed by my dream coming true.

277
00:20:04,974 --> 00:20:06,517
Please leave us alone.

278
00:20:11,731 --> 00:20:14,442
If you were to sum this
up, it'd be like this, right?

279
00:20:14,525 --> 00:20:17,028
Yes! You hit the nail on the head!

280
00:20:18,029 --> 00:20:21,115
Alright! Now's the time! Be sure to
spread the word wherever you're able!

281
00:20:21,199 --> 00:20:24,577
Didn't I just say to back off?!

282
00:20:24,661 --> 00:20:28,039
Whoa. Are they finally acting
like a normal, lovey- dovey couple?

283
00:20:28,122 --> 00:20:32,293
They were like this at the
after party, especially Kazehaya.

284
00:20:32,377 --> 00:20:35,338
You know... now that I'm getting a good look
at them, I don't know how I didn't notice

285
00:20:35,421 --> 00:20:38,174
this was even possible...

286
00:20:38,258 --> 00:20:41,135
...since they look so great together.

287
00:20:41,219 --> 00:20:44,931
- You think so?
- Man... They really are perfect.

288
00:20:58,486 --> 00:21:00,530
Oh yeah, that's right...

289
00:21:01,447 --> 00:21:03,950
Kurumi got her heart broken...

290
00:21:04,033 --> 00:21:09,747
...and it was Sadako who won the guy in
the end. Who would have guessed it?

291
00:22:27,158 --> 00:22:30,328
My new memories... have only just begun.

292
00:22:32,205 --> 00:22:34,582
Next time: "Important Person"
